.sp
ETag \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
An ETag is an opaque identifier assigned by a web server to a specific version of a resource found at a URL.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Checksum \-> (structure)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The checksum or digest of the object.
.sp
ChecksumCRC32 \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The Base64 encoded, 32\-bit \fBCRC32 checksum\fP of the object. This checksum is only be present if the checksum was uploaded with the object. When you use an API operation on an object that was uploaded using multipart uploads, this value may not be a direct checksum value of the full object. Instead, it\(aqs a calculation based on the checksum values of each individual part. For more information about how checksums are calculated with multipart uploads, see \fI\%Checking object integrity\fP in the \fIAmazon S3 User Guide\fP .
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
ChecksumCRC32C \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The Base64 encoded, 32\-bit \fBCRC32C\fP checksum of the object. This checksum is only present if the checksum was uploaded with the object. When you use an API operation on an object that was uploaded using multipart uploads, this value may not be a direct checksum value of the full object. Instead, it\(aqs a calculation based on the checksum values of each individual part. For more information about how checksums are calculated with multipart uploads, see \fI\%Checking object integrity\fP in the \fIAmazon S3 User Guide\fP .
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
ChecksumCRC64NVME \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The Base64 encoded, 64\-bit \fBCRC64NVME\fP checksum of the object. This checksum is present if the object was uploaded with the \fBCRC64NVME\fP checksum algorithm, or if the object was uploaded without a checksum (and Amazon S3 added the default checksum, \fBCRC64NVME\fP , to the uploaded object). For more information, see \fI\%Checking object integrity\fP in the \fIAmazon S3 User Guide\fP .
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
ChecksumSHA1 \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The Base64 encoded, 160\-bit \fBSHA1\fP digest of the object. This will only be present if the object was uploaded with the object. When you use the API operation on an object that was uploaded using multipart uploads, this value may not be a direct checksum value of the full object. Instead, it\(aqs a calculation based on the checksum values of each individual part. For more information about how checksums are calculated with multipart uploads, see \fI\%Checking object integrity\fP in the \fIAmazon S3 User Guide\fP .
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
ChecksumSHA256 \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The Base64 encoded, 256\-bit \fBSHA256\fP digest of the object. This will only be present if the object was uploaded with the object. When you use an API operation on an object that was uploaded using multipart uploads, this value may not be a direct checksum value of the full object. Instead, it\(aqs a calculation based on the checksum values of each individual part. For more information about how checksums are calculated with multipart uploads, see \fI\%Checking object integrity\fP in the \fIAmazon S3 User Guide\fP .
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
ChecksumType \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The checksum type that is used to calculate the object’s checksum value. For more information, see \fI\%Checking object integrity\fP in the \fIAmazon S3 User Guide\fP .
.sp
Possible values:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBCOMPOSITE\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBFULL_OBJECT\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
ObjectParts \-> (structure)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
A collection of parts associated with a multipart upload.
.sp
TotalPartsCount \-> (integer)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The total number of parts.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
PartNumberMarker \-> (integer)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The marker for the current part.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
NextPartNumberMarker \-> (integer)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
When a list is truncated, this element specifies the last part in the list, as well as the value to use for the \fBPartNumberMarker\fP request parameter in a subsequent request.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
MaxParts \-> (integer)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The maximum number of parts allowed in the response.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
IsTruncated \-> (boolean)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Indicates whether the returned list of parts is truncated. A value of \fBtrue\fP indicates that the list was truncated. A list can be truncated if the number of parts exceeds the limit returned in the \fBMaxParts\fP element.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Parts \-> (list)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
A container for elements related to a particular part. A response can contain zero or more \fBParts\fP elements.
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBGeneral purpose buckets\fP \- For \fBGetObjectAttributes\fP , if an additional checksum (including \fBx\-amz\-checksum\-crc32\fP , \fBx\-amz\-checksum\-crc32c\fP , \fBx\-amz\-checksum\-sha1\fP , or \fBx\-amz\-checksum\-sha256\fP ) isn\(aqt applied to the object specified in the request, the response doesn\(aqt return the \fBPart\fP element.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBDirectory buckets\fP \- For \fBGetObjectAttributes\fP , regardless of whether an additional checksum is applied to the object specified in the request, the response returns the \fBPart\fP element.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
